## Queue rules

- [ ] approved/ready; [~] assigned/unfinished; [x] delivered; [!] blocked; [-] draft/deferred.
- Task headings: `## [state] TASK-001 — Title`, with stable unique IDs.
- Older unique title-only headings and longer task bodies remain valid; no migration
  is required. Keep identities/history when simplifying an existing backlog.
- Declare dependencies as comma-separated IDs, or None. Keep referenced completed
  IDs in this file; the helper currently resolves dependencies here.
- Tech-lead plans/approves scope with the owner; overnight records assigned outcomes.
- Keep tasks short: outcome, meaningful acceptance, focused verification. Add Type,
  Branch, PR, or Blocked fields only when useful. Do not copy global process per task.
- Runner claims eligible tasks. Unfinished [~] resets to [ ] without discarding code
  or attempts. A fixable next step resumes normally; [!] needs owner recovery.
- [x] means verified delivery, not human merge. Dependency code must exist in the
  execution baseline. Record checkpoints in .opencode/progress.md, not status essays.

